# Opt72 (2026-10-30): STRATA_PF_MAC_QMIN_TOK=<tokens> (inert unless set; config D sets 3000): a prompt chunk, or a lockstep group (chunk tokens x chunks), under that many
# tokens does not queue the reads of every expert the GPU does not hold 3 layers ahead; it reads only the experts it routes to, on demand at each layer. A 1000-token
# chunk routes to ~219 cold experts per layer, about half of them already in the Mac LRU, while the read-ahead read all ~223 the LRU lacks (9,830 blobs = 18 GB per
# prompt on a ~2.3 GB/s SSD). Measured single arms: 1000 tok 8.51 -> 7.19 s (+18 %), 2.5K 10.17 -> 10.04 s, 400 and 8K unchanged, 0 GPU timeouts.
# Base: Strata v0.1.41 (fb58e0dbc839) + patches/strata/0001..0031. Source: campaign prefill.opt72.cpp (md5 0ba4f1cc), engine strata_o37j.
